{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1524633-custom-birthrights-thread","id":1524633,"title":"Custom Birthrights thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-28T06:00:08-07:00","id":1524633,"title":"Custom Birthrights thread","content":"Let us make a thread where we share our homebrew Birthrights, either completed or still at the idea stage.<br /> <br /> Here's one idea that's been occupying my head: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpe\" target=\"_blank\">Harp\u0113</a>.\u200b\u200b<br /> I've only came up with flavor text so far:<br /> <i>A sword with a sickle-shaped tip and forged by Gaea from adamant, the steel of the gods. The same weapon used by Cronus to castrate Ouranos, by Zeus to battle Typhon, and then finally, and most famously, by Perseus to behead the Gorgon Medusa. It is the blade of monster-slayers that can sever everything. However, whoever wields it is bound to become a target to the servants of Cronus, as the mad King of Titans longs to reclaim his old weapon, and, more importantly, it is the only thing in existence known to be capable of breaking his chains.</i><br /> <br /> I want to make it for my character concept, a Chosen Scion of Zeus who descends from the bloodline of Perseus, either at character creation or later in the campaign. What would be its rating and abilities, in your opinion?<br /> <br /> EDIT: another idea I had after posting: Charon as a Guide for a Scion of Hades or Persephone. Purviews he could teach would include Death (the Theoi's most iconic psychopomp), Water (his command over the waters of the Styx) and/or Prosperity (the whole thing with the coins).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 10-28-2023, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe